               "headline":  "Lumentum deal and AI-chip rout cut MRVL to $122; Q3 results due about 1 Dec",
               "summary":  "MRVL closed at $122.28 on 20 Nov 2026. That is 11.69% down on the day and about 29% below its 2 Nov close of $171.41. Two things caused the drop. On 2 Nov Marvell agreed to buy Lumentum for stock only (4.5 MRVL shares per Lumentum share, about $115B enterprise value), and BofA and TD Cowen downgraded the stock soon after. At the same time AI-chip stocks sold off across the sector. The business itself still looks healthy: Q3 revenue guidance of $3.15B was confirmed and the range narrowed, with results expected around 1 Dec.",
