               "caution":  "Momentum is still pointing down. Price is about $67 below the EMA 50, MACD is still falling, and the bands are so wide that 10% daily moves have been common. Oversold readings can last for weeks in a selloff. The Lumentum deal also changes what an MRVL share represents: the share count rises by roughly half, and the uncertainty runs until the first half of 2028. Shareholder votes, antitrust reviews (China included) and Lumentum\u0027s own results could all weigh on the stock. If the 1 Dec results or FY28 commentary disappoint, the $97.51 lower band and the February area near $70–74 are the next reference levels.",
               "opportunity":  "The selloff looks driven more by deal worries and sector sentiment than by any break in demand. On 2 Nov Marvell narrowed its Q3 range around $3.15B, and Q2 data center revenue grew 46%. RSI at 27.9 shows the selling is stretched. Most covering analysts kept Buy ratings even after cutting targets. If the deal closes, Marvell would own both the DSP and the laser inside AI optical links, which would deepen its optics moat. The 1 Dec report and the FY28 outlook are the next clear tests of whether the fundamentals still support that view.",
